[SIZE=7][B]BIBLE[/B][/SIZE]
[I]The boot loader RIPPS2 sets up. Signed, bound, and starting real PS2s.[/I]

[URL='https://github.com/akilluminati47/BIBLE/releases/latest'][B]Signed builds and SD2PSX BOOT card[/B][/URL]  |  [URL='https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/releases/latest/download/RIPPS2.elf']RIPPS2.elf (installs it for you)[/URL]  |  [URL='https://github.com/akilluminati47/BIBLE#readme']Every setting[/URL]  |  [URL='https://github.com/akilluminati47/BIBLE']Source (GPL-3)[/URL]  |  [URL='https://www.psx-place.com/threads/ripps2-a-ps2-front-end-in-one-elf-launch-disc-storage-memory-files.51316/']RIPPS2's thread[/URL]
[SIZE=2]Current: BIBLE 3282396, carried by RIPPS2 v1.3.9 beta[/SIZE][/CENTER]

[SIZE=3]BIBLE is akilluminati47's boot loader: a fork of saildot4k's [URL='https://github.com/saildot4k/PlayStation2-Basic-BootLoader-Extended']PS2BBL Extended[/URL], itself built on El Isra's [URL='https://github.com/israpps/PlayStation2-Basic-BootLoader']PS2BBL[/URL]. It sits on your memory card as the console's system update (or in the internal HDD's boot area) and, at power on, starts what you chose, RIPPS2 first. [B]Every build is signed by akilluminati47[/B], with kelftool on their own PC: nobody else's keys, nobody else's signing.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]Black, and fast[/B][/SIZE]
[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/main/media/b139/bible-race-6000-vs-0.gif[/IMG]
[SIZE=2]Both on Background: Black, no buttons, video mode AUTO, from BIBLE's first frame. Left, the 6000 ms countdown with the info line. Right, 0 ms.[/SIZE][/CENTER]

BIBLE can get out of your way. [B]Power-on Wait: 0 ms[/B] drops the countdown (PS2BBL Extended holds it at 500 ms or more), and [B]Background: Black[/B] with [B]Button Glyphs: None[/B] leaves the logo alone on black, so the hand-off into RIPPS2 reads as one piece. Those three are a menu pick in RIPPS2's Manage. For the last few seconds, add DISC_STOP = 0 to the settings file: BIBLE then leaves the disc drive alone at launch instead of waiting for it to answer, which took 3.3 s off this run.
[CODE]KEY_READ_WAIT_TIME = 0
BIBLE_BACKGROUND = BLANK
BIBLE_GLYPHS = 0
DISC_STOP = 0[/CODE]
[SIZE=2]A PCSX2 capture with RIPPS2 on a memory card, the slowest drive it can start from. The same 6.5 s of black load is cut from both sides, so the 6 s between them is the real gap. A faster drive shortens the load on both. With DISC_STOP = 0 a disc in the tray keeps spinning into RIPPS2.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]0 ms locks nothing away[/B][/SIZE]
With no countdown, a button held from power on still picks its entry. And when you can't remember what's on which button, hold [B]L2 + R2[/B] at power on: BIBLE stops before anything starts and shows what every button launches, whatever your splash settings, even with nothing on screen at all.
[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/main/media/b139/bible-keys-page-1080i.jpg[/IMG]
[SIZE=2]The launch keys page in 1080i: what each button starts, and START to go back[/SIZE][/CENTER]

Hold [B]TRIANGLE + CROSS[/B] at power on for the video mode page. It always opens in the console's own interlaced mode, so it is the way back from 720p or 1080i on a composite cable.
[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/BIBLE/main/assets/readme/bible-video-mode.png[/IMG][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]Or your own sky[/B][/SIZE]
[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/main/media/b139/bible-sky-red-green.jpg[/IMG]
[SIZE=2]Blood and Ectoplasm, two of RIPPS2's Color Themes, in 1080i[/SIZE][/CENTER]

[B]Background: Auto[/B] (the default) puts your RIPPS2 Color Theme's sky behind the logo when BIBLE starts RIPPS2, and goes black, like a plain boot loader, when it starts anything else. [B]Sky[/B] keeps it on for everything, and BIBLE_COLOR sets any sky you like. The same look in every video mode. At a launch the logo and buttons fade away and the sky stays until the console loads the next program, which blanks the screen (about 7 s in the lab with RIPPS2 on a memory card). RIPPS2 then comes up in the same video mode and colours.

[SIZE=5][B]Your splash[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][LEFT][B]Button Glyphs[/B]: none, the four face buttons, or all sixteen.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]Splash[/B]: off, the logo, or the logo with a sheet of every button you named.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]Info Line[/B]: the console's model, ROM, clock and countdown, off by default.[/LEFT]
[/LIST]
[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/main/media/b139/bible-button-names-1080i.jpg[/IMG]
[SIZE=2]Splash: Logo and Names[/SIZE][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]Made to start RIPPS2[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][LEFT][B]The boot sound, primed[/B]: with RIPPS2's Boot Sound On (fast), boot.adp sits beside BIBLE's settings on the card and is read before any drive starts. No sound file is the fastest boot.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]Video modes up to 1080i[/B]: AUTO (RIPPS2's own mode), NTSC, PAL, 480p, 576p, 720p and 1080i, with widescreen for the 4:3 ones.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]Four builds[/B]: memory card (memory cards and USB), MMCE (SD2PSX and MemCard PRO 2), MX4SIO, and the internal HDD's boot area.[/LEFT]
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Install it[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][LEFT][B]With RIPPS2 (nothing to download)[/B]: RIPPS2.elf carries all four signed builds. Settings > General > Boot Loader > [B]Manage[/B] picks the one that reaches where RIPPS2 lives, has the console bind it to your card, moves whatever was there into a backup folder (nothing is deleted) and writes BIBLE's settings file, starting RIPPS2 first.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]Already have BIBLE?[/B] Manage opens a BIBLE menu. [B]UPDATE BIBLE[/B] binds the newest over an older one in place, and every setting above is one pick away.[/LEFT]
[/LIST]
[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/main/media/b139/new-01-bible-menu.jpg[/IMG]
[SIZE=2]Manage's BIBLE menu in RIPPS2 1.3.9[/SIZE][/CENTER]
[LIST]
[*][LEFT][B]SD2PSX owners[/B]: [URL='https://github.com/akilluminati47/BIBLE/releases/latest/download/BIBLE-SD2PSX-BootCard-3282396.zip']BIBLE-SD2PSX-BootCard-3282396.zip[/URL] is a ready BOOT card with BIBLE already bound. Keep a copy of your own BootCard-1.mcd, copy this one over it, put RIPPS2.ELF in the SD card's APPS folder, power on.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT][B]With KELFBinder[/B]: [URL='https://github.com/akilluminati47/BIBLE/releases/latest/download/BIBLE-signed-3282396.zip']BIBLE-signed-3282396.zip[/URL] has SYSTEM.XLF (memory card), MMCE/SYSTEM.XLF, MX4SIO/SYSTEM.XLF and HSYSTEM.XLF (HDD), with their SHA-256s.[/LEFT]
[/LIST]
[SIZE=2]A memory card KELF only starts once a console has bound it to that card: Manage and KELFBinder do this as they install it. Copying the file onto a card by hand does not make it boot. The binding is the console's own MechaCon at work; RIPPS2 boots KELFBinder's IOPRP image for that step and holds no keys.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]Its settings[/B][/SIZE]
One text file on the card, [B]mc?:/SYS-CONF/PS2BBL.INI[/B] (read first; else PS2BBL/CONFIG.INI on a card, USB, MMCE or the HDD). RIPPS2's Manage writes it and its BIBLE menu changes it, one line at a time, keeping your notes; Memory Files opens it as text. Lines starting with # are notes, and every key is optional.
[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Key[/TH][TH]In RIPPS2's menu[/TH][TH]What it does[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]KEY_READ_WAIT_TIME[/TD][TD]Power-on Wait[/TD][TD]How long (ms) a button held at power on can pick its entry; 0 is allowed[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]BIBLE_BACKGROUND[/TD][TD]Background[/TD][TD]AUTO (RIPPS2's sky when BIBLE starts RIPPS2, else black), SKY or BLANK[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]LOGO_DISPLAY[/TD][TD]Splash[/TD][TD]0 nothing on screen, 2 the logo, 3 the logo and each button's name[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]BIBLE_GLYPHS[/TD][TD]Button Glyphs[/TD][TD]The buttons under the logo: 0 none, 1 the face buttons, 2 all sixteen[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]BIBLE_INFO[/TD][TD]Info Line[/TD][TD]1: console model, ROM, clock and countdown[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]VIDEO_MODE[/TD][TD]Video Mode[/TD][TD]AUTO, NTSC, PAL, 480P, 576P, 720P or 1080I[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]BIBLE_WIDESCREEN[/TD][TD]Widescreen[/TD][TD]AUTO (RIPPS2's Widescreen, else the PS2's 16:9 setting), ON or OFF[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]DISC_STOP[/TD][TD]the file[/TD][TD]1 stops the disc at launch and waits for the drive (the default), 0 leaves it alone[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]BIBLE_COLOR[/TD][TD]the file[/TD][TD]The sky's top, horizon and floor colours (0D0000,700400,170000); unset, the Color Theme RIPPS2 saved[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]NAME_<button>, LK_<button>_E1 to E10[/TD][TD]the file[/TD][TD]What each button starts (AUTO: no button held), the first entry that exists. $OSDSYS the browser, $CDVD the disc, $CREDITS BIBLE's credits[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[SIZE=5][B]Tested on a real PS2[/B][/SIZE]
[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Console[/TH][TH]Card[/TH][TH]What[/TH][TH]Result[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]SCPH-39001 (USA, fat)[/TD][TD]SD2PSX BOOT card, slot 0[/TD][TD]MMCE build a1ffb0b, bound by KELFBinder[/TD][TD]BIBLE's splash, then RIPPS2[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]the same[/TD][TD]the same[/TD][TD]a1ffb0b, bound by RIPPS2 1.3.8's Manage[/TD][TD]BIBLE's splash, then RIPPS2[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]the same[/TD][TD]the same[/TD][TD]3282396, bound over it by RIPPS2 1.3.9's UPDATE BIBLE[/TD][TD]BIBLE's splash, then RIPPS2[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]the same[/TD][TD]the same[/TD][TD]Power-on Wait 0 ms, Button Glyphs None and Background Black set from the BIBLE menu[/TD][TD]Written to the settings file[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]
[B]Wanted most[/B]: a genuine Sony memory card, a MemCard PRO 2, MX4SIO, the HDD build, slims, PAL and Japanese consoles. Tell us here or [URL='https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2/issues']open an issue[/URL] with your console model, your card and a photo of anything odd.

[SIZE=5][B]If something goes wrong[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][LEFT]Hold a button at power on to start something else. In the settings file Manage writes: TRIANGLE the browser, START a disc, CIRCLE what was there before BIBLE. L2 + R2 shows them all.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT]When nothing a button points at can be found, BIBLE says so: START tries the launch keys again, R1 + START opens rescue mode.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT]In RIPPS2, Manage's card list has [B]RESTORE SLOT n'S OLD BOOT LOADER[/B]: it puts back what BIBLE replaced, and BIBLE moves aside. Nothing is deleted.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT]On an SD2PSX, the BOOT card is a file: copy your own BootCard-1.mcd back from the PC.[/LEFT]
[*][LEFT]A card the console would not bind is left as it was. An SD2PSX can stop answering after a refused bind: turn the console off and on.[/LEFT]
[/LIST]

[SPOILER="Changes"]
[B]3282396[/B] (with RIPPS2 1.3.9): BIBLE_BACKGROUND, boot.adp beside BIBLE's settings (its hand-off to RIPPS2 in memory has passed in the lab only), RIPPS2 first in the built-in defaults, RIPPS2's settings read from mc?:/RIPPS2 when RIPPS2 lives on an SD2PSX, USB or the HDD.
[B]a1ffb0b[/B] (with RIPPS2 1.3.8): the MMCE and MX4SIO builds start again (f31c8d5's waited on a memory card driver that never loaded: a black screen at power on).
[B]f31c8d5[/B] (with RIPPS2 1.3.4): the first signed BIBLE: its splash, the launch keys and video mode pages, the HD modes and widescreen.
[/SPOILER]

